bitnet-b1.58: use squared-ReLU FFN only for the 2B-4T model (30 layers)

BitNet-b1.58-2B-4T uses ReLU^2 in its FFN (hidden_act "relu2"), but the b158 arch reused
the 3B bitnet graph, which is SiLU, giving looping/garbage output. The 1bitLLM models
(bitnet_b1_58-large/3B, hidden_act "silu") share the same arch and must stay on SiLU.

diff --git a/src/models/bitnet.cpp b/src/models/bitnet.cpp
index 985c8d6fc..24ba5623e 100644
--- a/src/models/bitnet.cpp
+++ b/src/models/bitnet.cpp
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@ llama_model_bitnet::graph::graph(const llama_model & model, const llm_graph_para
                 model.layers[il].ffn_gate, NULL, model.layers[il].ffn_gate_s,
                 NULL,                      NULL, NULL,
                 NULL,
-                LLM_FFN_SILU, LLM_FFN_PAR, il);
+                (model.arch == LLM_ARCH_BITNET_B158 && model.type == LLM_TYPE_2B) ? LLM_FFN_RELU_SQR : LLM_FFN_SILU, LLM_FFN_PAR, il);
         cb(cur, "ffn_sub_out", il);
 
         cur = build_norm(cur,
